WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:01.944
- I feel like I'm at the worst

00:00:01.944 --> 00:00:03.659
like wedding cake tasting
(man laughs)

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:05.142
in the whole world.

00:00:05.142 --> 00:00:06.758
- It's like the wedding of the apocalypse.

00:00:06.758 --> 00:00:09.341
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.386 --> 00:00:11.795
- When I think of survival food

00:00:11.795 --> 00:00:13.669
I automatically think I'm gonna eat a bug.

00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:15.895
- Survival food is what you keep in your

00:00:15.895 --> 00:00:19.276
apocalypse bunker, like a can
of beans, or some Twinkies.

00:00:19.276 --> 00:00:21.523
- Fish that you grabbed with
your hands from a stream

00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:22.356
when you're lost.

00:00:22.356 --> 00:00:23.478
- See I'm a past boy scout

00:00:23.478 --> 00:00:25.292
and survival food is like MREs,

00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:26.853
which is meals ready to eat.

00:00:26.853 --> 00:00:28.827
- I'm very nervous, I have no idea

00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:32.577
what's in this food,
what we're about to eat.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.802
- It doesn't look bad.
- Yeah.

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:38.629
- Oh so it's just a
packet that's freeze dried

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:40.319
and then you add water into it.

00:00:40.319 --> 00:00:42.530
- These chunks look like cat food to me.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.270
- Survival food or
probably college food too.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.124
(woman laughs)

00:00:46.124 --> 00:00:47.725
Did a lot at college.

00:00:47.725 --> 00:00:48.558
- Cheers.

00:00:52.568 --> 00:00:53.651
- This is pretty good.

00:00:53.651 --> 00:00:54.703
- I mean it's got flavor.

00:00:54.703 --> 00:00:56.402
- The chicken kinda tastes like fish.

00:00:56.402 --> 00:00:57.683
- Maybe airplane good.

00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.539
- I mean, I'm like going
back for another bite.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:00.372
- Right.

00:01:00.372 --> 00:01:02.434
- I mean if I was on a budget,

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:03.323
if I only had a few dollars.

00:01:03.323 --> 00:01:04.156
- I think I need it now.

00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:04.989
(woman and man laugh)

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:06.122
- Can I eat it all?

00:01:06.122 --> 00:01:07.088
Alright, it's pretty good.

00:01:07.088 --> 00:01:08.673
- I would definitely eat
this chicken and rice

00:01:08.673 --> 00:01:10.330
before I would eat a person.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.830
- Okay, same.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.476
- It doesn't look like
any food I've ever seen.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.873
- I feel like this looks
like astronaut food, maybe.

00:01:19.873 --> 00:01:20.930
- Are we gonna break a tooth?

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.089
- I think if a crumb
cake and a rock fucked...

00:01:23.089 --> 00:01:24.164
(record screeches)

00:01:24.164 --> 00:01:28.076
- Is it weird I imagined that in my head?

00:01:28.076 --> 00:01:29.604
- Oh my, it's so hard.

00:01:29.604 --> 00:01:31.187
- It's really hard.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.187
- A little tough to bite into.

00:01:35.187 --> 00:01:36.384
But it's got flavor.

00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:37.618
- Like a strawberry Laffy Taffy

00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:38.752
but like someone like messed up

00:01:38.752 --> 00:01:41.108
and forgot to put all
the strawberry in there.

00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:42.264
- I don't know it doesn't actually...

00:01:42.264 --> 00:01:43.097
- No.

00:01:43.097 --> 00:01:45.142
- It wants to.
- It's got like chalk flavor.

00:01:45.142 --> 00:01:48.301
- I can't even break it in half.

00:01:48.301 --> 00:01:50.265
- It is unbreakable.

00:01:50.265 --> 00:01:53.360
- I'm a big dude, I can't even.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.677
- I guess if like the zombies are coming,

00:01:54.677 --> 00:01:56.242
you could throw this at them

00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:57.936
and it would like hurt them a little bit.

00:01:57.936 --> 00:01:58.934
- That is very true.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:02.184
This could also be doubled as a weapon.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:05.290
- Is this cheese?

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.999
- It looks like the crust of like a pie

00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:09.610
that didn't want to finish.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.389
- It looks like a fry and
Parmesan cheese fucked.

00:02:12.389 --> 00:02:14.445
- Awe, that's pretty good.
- Yeah.

00:02:14.445 --> 00:02:15.664
- It's softer.

00:02:15.664 --> 00:02:19.073
- Much softer than that other thing.

00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:21.810
- This is something you'd find
in like the 99 cent store.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:22.682
- This is weirdly good.

00:02:22.682 --> 00:02:24.538
I feel like I would like snack on this.

00:02:24.538 --> 00:02:27.090
- If you had some peanut butter on this,

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.486
that would probably be really good.

00:02:28.486 --> 00:02:30.123
- I'd probably go and look for some fish

00:02:30.123 --> 00:02:31.364
in the stream or something.

00:02:31.364 --> 00:02:33.402
- I think I would probably
eat this while I was looking

00:02:33.402 --> 00:02:35.652
for the fish in the stream.

00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:39.461
- This looks like the bag
that dog treats come in.

00:02:39.461 --> 00:02:40.389
(man and woman laugh)

00:02:40.389 --> 00:02:41.222
- What?

00:02:41.222 --> 00:02:42.055
- What is in this?

00:02:42.055 --> 00:02:43.277
- Is it a bug?

00:02:43.277 --> 00:02:44.465
(man and woman laugh)

00:02:44.465 --> 00:02:45.884
- Survival tabs?

00:02:45.884 --> 00:02:47.832
- Full meals in one little piece of candy.

00:02:47.832 --> 00:02:49.924
- It smells like lip gloss for children.

00:02:49.924 --> 00:02:51.583
- Do you smell lip gloss
for children often?

00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:52.416
- Yeah.

00:02:52.416 --> 00:02:53.785
- This is looks like what I throw in...

00:02:53.785 --> 00:02:55.350
like with my laundry.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.682
- I ain't got a chewy.

00:02:56.682 --> 00:02:57.515
- It's bad.

00:02:57.515 --> 00:02:58.439
- It's real bad.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:03:00.068
- I don't like this one.

00:03:00.068 --> 00:03:02.296
- It's very chalky like it looks.

00:03:02.296 --> 00:03:03.613
Gets better as you nibble.

00:03:03.613 --> 00:03:04.446
- Crunchy.

00:03:04.446 --> 00:03:06.005
- It's a creaminess, but
you're like why is it creamy

00:03:06.005 --> 00:03:07.397
and there's nothing creamy about it

00:03:07.397 --> 00:03:08.445
when it was in my hand.

00:03:08.445 --> 00:03:11.264
- I'd rather eat a person than eat this,

00:03:11.264 --> 00:03:12.517
like I'm gonna eat my neighbor

00:03:12.517 --> 00:03:14.788
before I'm eating these creamy tabs.

00:03:14.788 --> 00:03:16.586
- There are some nutrients in it.

00:03:16.586 --> 00:03:18.710
- My mouth feels weird now.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.474
- My mouth feels like a survivor.

00:03:21.474 --> 00:03:23.145
- You can survive three weeks without

00:03:23.145 --> 00:03:24.624
having any food in your body.

00:03:24.624 --> 00:03:26.152
- I could survive a few hours.

00:03:26.152 --> 00:03:28.664
- I can't even like
install an A/C you know?

00:03:28.664 --> 00:03:29.663
Although I will say that like

00:03:29.663 --> 00:03:31.989
pretty okay with like eating bugs.

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:35.057
- After you've been hiking
for like eight or 10 hours,

00:03:35.057 --> 00:03:37.480
you would literally eat like dog crap.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.313
- Would you?

00:03:38.313 --> 00:03:39.859
- People have eaten people before

00:03:39.859 --> 00:03:40.911
because they're hungry.

00:03:40.911 --> 00:03:41.974
- Cause they hiked for eight hours?

00:03:41.974 --> 00:03:42.929
- Cause they had to survive,

00:03:42.929 --> 00:03:43.826
cause they hiked for eight hours,

00:03:43.826 --> 00:03:47.076
you know I have a sensational appetite.

